  "summary": "Postinstall fetches and executes remote shell script from third-party GitHub repository",
  "details": "The package includes scripts/dependency-manager.js which invokes execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh | sh') to download and execute a shell installer from a mutable master branch of a third-party GitHub repository (rtk-ai/rtk) at install time. The script also makes network calls to https://www.rtk-ai.app and reads host information via os.homedir() and process.platform. The fetched install.sh comes from a floating branch reference with no pinning, hash verification, or signature check, so its contents can change at any time and execute arbitrary code on the installer's machine. The package name (@leejungkiin/awkit) does not correspond to the rtk-ai publisher whose script is being executed, and the package documents itself around AWK tooling rather than as an rtk-ai installer, creating a publisher/purpose mismatch. Additional shipped code (bin/awk.js, scripts/model-manager.js) combines child_process with outbound HTTP/curl operations.",
